The Sighurt contributors have modified the files that came from Oxide. The
codebase has been restructured into a browser (sighurt-browser, sighurt-core,
sighurt-ui), an engine protocol (sighurt-ipc) and separate engine processes.
The WASM engine (sighurt-engine-wasm), the guest SDK (sighurt-sdk, formerly
oxide-sdk), the GPUI chrome, the documentation and the example apps are
derived from Oxide's source. The git history records the individual changes.

The WASM guest ABI keeps Oxide's "oxide" import module name, so applications
built for Oxide run unchanged in Sighurt's WASM engine.

sighurt-engine-servo (the sig-servo binary) is licensed under Apache-2.0 AND
MPL-2.0. Its file src/rendering.rs is adapted from rendering_context.rs in
the Servo project (https://github.com/servo/servo) and remains under the
Mozilla Public License, Version 2.0 (https://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/).
sig-servo also links Servo, which is licensed under MPL-2.0.
